Z||000000||TRiAD||12-24-2001||01:55 PM||||Please post sources for 3800SC swaps, engines, parts, mods, etc, relating to the 3800SC. <P>If you happen to own one, please post the good and bad points you've noticed with your swap. <P>I'd be looking primarilly for a manual, but info on either is OK. <P>If you're close to me (IL) and know of a gathering early spring or sooner that you will be at, and would be willing to take me for a ride, please let me know that as well. <BR> <BR>It took me 18 months to research the Fiero to the point where I could feel comfortable buying one, now I'm researching engine options, at the moment; 3800SC only. I'll look into others later. <P>I'm wanting to retain a weight balance, streetability, while approaching 300-350HP on a manual. <P>Let's see what you got.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks for any and all info you can provide.<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAAAMsSN*Wryq60N*CeWB!hXjfeIaMEc1YxPH9aPzaIXm!17ZpdBFE0Yk*d*dHNFG*GR3SFyLa8KJgh1IKe2Q/xmas-sig.jpg">       <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="red">Merry Christmas!</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B><BR>Photoshop rendition of planned modifications<BR>AIM ~ Michael Blue 72</I></FONT>||||reg||1
