Z||000005||Formula88||12-24-2001||10:43 PM||||Anyone know how the all iron 3800SC compares in weight to a Small Block Chevy with Aluminum Heads?||||reg||5
Z||000006||Wannabe||12-24-2001||11:43 PM||||SBC with Al heads wp and intake is around 490lbs. 3800 SC is around 440. There is talk of Al heads being availble soon for the 3800. These should save about 40-50lbs.||||reg||1
Z||000007||AgaricX||12-25-2001||02:56 AM||||The swap is pretty straigtforward.  I had some issues with wiring, but this was my first engine swap gig.  I swapped out the auto tranny for a 5spd isuzu.  DEFINITELY the way to go.<P>FieroX is really the best authority I've found in this swap.  He knows more than I do... and I'm pushing 280HP and LOVING it.  I'm wathcing his site to see how I can improve my ride.<P>Bottom line - you can't do any better for speed / price / reliability.<P>Next up: Northstar Manual.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.agaric.net/fiero/AgaricX.jpg">  <BR>'85 SE 3800SC 5 Spd<BR>I WANT A FASTBACK!!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||fieroX||12-25-2001||03:37 AM||||thanks for the kind words AgaricX, but I dont consider myself a real authority yet.  My biggest resource is one of my best friends who put the 3800 sc in his 91 chevy lumina see <A HREF="http://www.luminasupercharged.com." TARGET=_blank>www.luminasupercharged.com.</A>   <BR>All of us are really learning together, so to try and take some of the confusion out of the swap I decided to set up a website to detail the swap.  BTW, what you see on my site now, is to show Im getting somewhere on the swap, but it is only about 2% complete.<BR>I cant wait to smoke some naysayers!<P>------------------<BR>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroX.com" TARGET=_blank>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif">    </A><BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroX.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroX.com</A><BR>coming soon L67 powered 87 notchback to smoke you with!<p>[This message has been edited by fieroX (edited 12-25-2001).]||||reg||1
